\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] FPreExtrapos
\item[* relevant examples:]
\item[* language:] English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_SentOKrules
\item[* date of creation:] 5-APR-1989 14:36:41  
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:]
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] speed filter, to prevent extraposed sentences from not being put 
back where they belong. In case of subject sentences of predrel/XPs, 
the extraposed sentence must remain where it is until RXppExtrapSubjSentSubst
puts it back into subject position.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
